::kind(api)

::meta{crate: tomet-benches, dependencies: list(tomet-config, tomet-formatter, tomet-parser, tomet-tests), dependents: list()}

=[tomet-benches]

==[tomet-benches]

Inputs shared by every criterion benchmark in this package. Each input is
checked against the real parser before anything is timed, so a bench can
never end up measuring an error path.

==[Sources]

- ("`fixtures`") The frozen in-repo corpus from `tomet-tests`; always there.
- ("`synth_doc`") One document generated by `tomet-synth` at a chosen size.
The same bytes for the same arguments (fixed [`SEED`]).
- ("`external_sets`") Real data from a `tomet-corpus` checkout. Present only
when `TOMET_CORPUS_DIR` points at one; otherwise empty,
never an error.

`tomet-synth` writes plain text and knows nothing of this repository, so the
check that its output parses lives here, in `assert_parses`.

==[Running]

```text
cargo bench -p tomet-benches                     # fixtures + synthetic
TOMET_CORPUS_DIR=../tomet-corpus cargo bench -p tomet-benches   # + real data
TOMET_BENCH_LARGE=1 cargo bench -p tomet-benches                # + 1 MB documents
cargo bench -p tomet-benches -- --test           # run each bench once, no timing
```

==[Structs]

===[struct Input]

==[Enums]

===[enum Flavor]

==[Functions]

===[fn fixtures]

Every fixture the parser is expected to accept.

===[fn synth_doc]

One synthetic document of roughly `bytes` bytes (it overshoots by at most
one block).

===[fn external_sets]

Real data sets from `TOMET_CORPUS_DIR`, as `(set name, files)`.

A set that is missing, or whose files all fail to parse, is left out. A
file that fails to parse is dropped and counted on stderr: real data is
allowed to be imperfect, a benchmark is not allowed to time its failure.

===[fn assert_parses]

Panics, naming the input, unless `tomet-parser` accepts it.

===[fn total_bytes]

Total size of a set, for throughput.

==[Constants]

===[const SEED]

Seed of every synthetic document. Changing it voids every recorded
baseline, exactly like changing the generator's stream does.

===[const CORPUS_DIR_ENV]

Environment variable naming a `tomet-corpus` checkout.
